g" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siglo XX mine</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Siglo XX is a large tin mine at Llallagua in the department of Potosí, Bolivia, developed by Simón Patiño in the early twentieth century and nationalised in 1952.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigmaringen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigmaringen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigmaringen</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigmaringen is a town on the upper Danube in Baden-Württemberg, Germany, dominated by a castle on a rock above the river.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigmund-freud"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigmund-freud.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigmund Freud</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigmund Freud was an Austrian neurologist who founded psychoanalysis, working in Vienna from the late nineteenth century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigmundur-brestisson"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigmundur-brestisson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigmundur Brestisson</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigmundur Brestisson was a Faroese chieftain and the central hero of the Færeyinga saga.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/signoria-of-florence"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/signoria-of-florence.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Signoria of Florence</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Signoria was the chief executive body of the Republic of Florence, composed of the priors of the guilds and, from 1293, the Gonfaloniere of Justice.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigtuna"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigtuna.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigtuna</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigtuna is a town on Lake Mälaren north-west of Stockholm, founded around 980 as a royal centre.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigurd-eysteinsson"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigurd-eysteinsson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigurd Eysteinsson</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigurd Eysteinsson, called the Mighty, was according to the Orkneyinga saga the first Earl of Orkney, in the late 9th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigurd-syr"><span class="enc-name">Sigurd Syr</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigurd Syr was a petty king of Ringerike in eastern Norway in the early eleventh century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigurd-the-crusader"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigurd-the-crusader.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigurd the Crusader</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigurd I, known as Sigurd the Crusader (Jorsalfar), was King of Norway from 1103 to 1130.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sihl"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sihl.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sihl</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sihl is a river in central Switzerland, about 73 kilometres long, which rises in the canton of Schwyz, flows through the Sihlsee reservoir and runs north to join…</span></a></li></ul>
